  "rules": [
    "Match rest poses first - retarget quality is dominated by rest alignment.",
    "SOMA rest is a T-pose, this Mixamo rig rests in an A-pose: Rig Match Pose has real work to do.",
    "Use the SOMA rest branch as the source rest, not frame 1.",
    "Do not map SOMA 'Root' as the locomotion root; it is static. Locomotion lives on 'Hips'.",
    "Disable automatic bounds-based scaling where it fights the explicit 0.01 BVH scale.",
    "Prefer the sparse fbik_targets set over driving every mapped joint.",
    "Leaf joints (mixamorig:*_End, finger *4) exist only on the animated branch - never map them.",
    "Never let Rig Match Pose bbox-scale the target (bboxmatch): it resizes the Mixamo rig to the SOMA bounds. Size matching belongs on the source, by leg-length ratio."
  ],
